gaJd(){return"YTD"},
gKh(){return"Personal IRR"},
gaJe(){return"Internal Rate of Return (IRR) \u2014 your personal annualised return, adjusted for the exact timing of every buy and sell.\n\nUnlike simple P/L%, IRR accounts for how long each amount was invested. A 20% IRR means your money grew at 20% per year on average.\n\nAccounts for the exact timing and size of every cash flow in your portfolio."},
gaJf(){return"Your annualised return accounting for when each investment was made."},
gaJg(){return"Add owned stocks to see position sizes."},
gaJh(){return"Shows how concentrated your portfolio is and how much dry powder you have.\n\n\u2022 Position sizes \u2014 each stock as a % of total portfolio value\n\u2022 Cash / Liquidity \u2014 uninvested cash you can deploy\n\nLarge single positions increase risk. A cash buffer lets you act on opportunities.\n\nWhat your cash affects: it counts toward your Total wealth and your concentration % (it shows as a slice here), and nothing else. It does NOT change your returns (IRR), risk metrics (VaR, Sharpe, beta) or the equity curve \u2014 those are based on your holdings only."},
aJi(a,b,c){return"Lens: your own closed rounds with your own thresholds \u2014 win \u2265 "+c+", loss \u2264 "+b+", floor "+a+" rounds per trait. Verdicts are tendencies computed by rule, not grades, and never buy or sell advice."},
gaJk(){return"Profitability"},
gaJj(){return"Profit on everything you put in, including the cash you got back from sells & dividends."},
gaJl(){return"A snapshot of your portfolio's fundamental characteristics.\n\n\u2022 Company Size \u2014 market cap buckets (Mega/Large/Mid/Small Cap)\n\u2022 Workforce Scale \u2014 employee headcount per stock\n\u2022 Valuation \u2014 simple average P/E vs market norms (see the value-weighted P/E in By Asset Class)\n\u2022 Income \u2014 dividend yield distribution\n\u2022 Profitability \u2014 profit margin range across holdings"},
aJm(a){return"\u03b2 "+a+" (excluded)"},
gaJn(){return"Biggest Winners"},
gaJo(){return'Biggest Winners \u2014 P/L% \xd7 position weight\n\nCombines how well a stock performed with how much of your shown portfolio it represents.\nA +40% gain on 20% of your portfolio outranks a +40% gain on 2%.\n\nWeight is each holding\'s value in your display currency, relative to the stocks currently shown (tag filter affects this). A holding with no exchange rate is left out and shows "no rate".'},
gaJp(){return"Compounding"},
gaJq(){return"Compounding Quality \u2014 Annualised return (CAGR)\n\nHow fast each position compounds per year.\nRequires at least 90 days of holding \u2014 newer positions sort to the bottom."},
aJr(a){return"  \xb7  "+a+" div"},
gaJs(){return'Income Score \u2014 Dividends on the shares you still hold \xf7 Cost of those shares \xd7 100\n\nHow much income your current position has generated relative to what you put in.\nDividends earned by shares you have since sold are not in the score (the amount shown is everything received).\nStocks with no dividends logged score 0.\nStocks with no investment recorded sort to the bottom, and so does a stock with a dividend whose exchange rate has not arrived yet (it shows "\u2014").'},
gaJt(){return"Add at least 2 owned stocks to see rankings."},
gaJu(){return"no beta"},
gaJv(){return"no cost basis"},
gaJw(){return"no dividends"},
gaJx(){return"no live price"},
gaJB(){return"none on shares held"},
gaJy(){return"no P/E"},
gaJz(){return"no purchase date"},
aJA(a){return a+"  \xb7  no rate"},
aJC(a,b){return a+"  \xb7  "+b+"% of shown"},
aJD(a){return"P/E "+a},
aJE(a){return a+" received"},
gaJF(){return"Return vs Risk"},
gaJG(){return"Return vs Risk \u2014 P/L% \xf7 Beta\n\nHigher = better return for the volatility taken on.\nA stock up 30% with beta 0.8 scores better than one up 30% with beta 1.5.\n\nStocks with no beta data, or negative beta (inverse ETFs), sort to the bottom."},
gaJH(){return"Total Return"},
gaJI(){return'Total Return \u2014 (Unrealized P/L + Dividends on the shares you still hold) \xf7 Cost of those shares \xd7 100\n\nTrue all-in return on your current position, including both price appreciation and income.\nDividends earned by shares you have since sold belong to their realised P/L, not to this score \u2014 the amount beside each row is everything received.\nStocks with no investment recorded sort to the bottom, and so does a stock with a dividend whose exchange rate has not arrived yet (it shows "\u2014").'},
aJJ(a){return a+" total"},
gaJK(){return"<90 days held"},
gaJL(){return"Value Score"},
gaJM(){return"Value Score \u2014 100 \xf7 P/E ratio\n\nLower P/E = higher score = potentially cheaper relative to earnings.\nA P/E of 10 scores 10.0; a P/E of 50 scores 2.0.\n\nStocks with no P/E data (ETFs, no-earnings companies) sort to the bottom."},
aJN(a){return"  \xb7  "+a+"% yield"},
ga9g(){return"Read your profile"},
gaJY(){return"Real"},
aK1(a){return"Splits your total profit/loss into money you have LOCKED IN and money still FLOATING.\n\n\u2022 Locked In (Realized) \u2014 P/L on shares you have already sold (plus dividends attributed to them). This is booked; market moves no longer change it.\n\u2022 Floating (Unrealized) \u2014 P/L on shares you still hold. It moves with the market until you sell.\n\nBoth are in "+a+": each holding's result is measured in its own currency and converted at today's rate.\n\nThis Total P/L is not the Portfolio Summary's. It also counts fully sold holdings and the dividends on sold shares, and it leaves out how exchange rates have moved since you bought \u2014 so the two can differ.\n\nDividends on shares you still hold are not counted here (Real vs Paper counts them)."},
gaJZ(){return'This card uses the "Return on cost" lens.\n\nReturn on cost = your profit \xf7 the cost of everything it was earned on: the shares you still hold plus the shares you have sold. It answers: "how much has my money made on what I put at risk?"\n\nThe "Cost" row is that cost. P/L, Cost and Value are converted at today\'s exchange rates.\n\nThe "Do I Beat the Market?" card shows no return percentage. Its "You made" is your profit in money: what you hold today, plus the cash you got back from sells and dividends, minus everything you put in \u2014 with each trade at its own date\'s exchange rate where one exists, so it can differ from the P/L here.\n\nFor a yearly rate that accounts for when you invested, see the Personal IRR card.'},
gaK_(){return"Return on cost \u2014 profit \xf7 the cost of everything it was earned on. Includes sold positions and the dividends on shares you have sold (not those on shares you still hold), so it can differ from the Portfolio tab (which shows open holdings only)."},
gaK0(){return"Return on cost \u2014 profit \xf7 the cost of everything it was earned on. Start a Paper Portfolio to compare a risk-free test run against your real money side by side."},
gaK2(){return"Noted rounds did worse."},
aK3(a,b){return"Rounds with a written reason ended at a median "+a+", un-noted ones at "+b+"."},
gaK4(){return"Noted rounds did better."},
a9h(a){return"Becomes measurable at "+a+" noted rounds."},
gaK5(){return"No round carries a written reason yet."},
aK6(a,b){return a+" of your rounds carry a written reason, "+b+" of your sales."},
aK7(a,b,c){var s=null,r=A.av(a,s,this.a,s,"round","rounds",s,s)
return"The last "+A.w(c)+" months hold "+a+" "+r+" \u2014 under the floor of "+b+", so every trait reads \u2014 there."},
